/** \mainpage GPSDataAdder Code Documentation

\section scope Scope

GPSDataAdder is an offline GPS L1 C/A IQ-file augmentation tool. It reads local
little-endian complex64 recordings, generates deterministic synthetic GPS
signals, and can add a multi-satellite position relocation overlay for decoder
testing. The project deliberately avoids SDR control, transmission, live stream
handling, or network assistance.

This Doxygen set documents the Python package under \c app, repository support
files, and the high-level design notes below. Build it with:

\code{.ps1}
doxygen Doxyfile
\endcode

Generated HTML is written under \c docs/doxygen-output/html and is ignored by
Git. The Doxygen source files and Python docstrings are the committed
documentation artifacts.

\section workflow End-To-End Workflow

1. \c app/main.py starts either the PySide6 GUI or the CLI fallback.
2. \c app/gui/main_window.py collects file paths, signal settings, processing
   settings, and position-overlay parameters.
3. \c app/gui/workers.py moves detection, planning, and file writing into
   background threads so the GUI stays responsive.
4. \c app/dsp/synthetic_satellite.py estimates amplitude, generates one
   deterministic GPS L1 C/A channel, and writes blockwise complex64 output.
5. \c app/dsp/tow_detect.py optionally asks the sibling Fraunhofer_FHR project
   for fast TOW evidence from real captures.
6. \c app/dsp/relocation_overlay.py asks Fraunhofer_FHR for baseline PVT,
   decoded received PRNs, ephemeris templates, code tracking, and satellite
   geometry, then writes stronger received-PRN replicas for a target position.
7. \c app/tests keeps C/A generation, LNAV parity, synthetic-file writing, and
   relocation-overlay behavior covered by focused pytest cases.

\section dsp DSP Modules

\subsection gpsca app/dsp/gps_ca.py

Generates GPS L1 C/A PRN chips for PRNs 1 through 32 and samples local code
replicas at arbitrary sample rates and code rates.

\subsection lnav app/dsp/lnav.py

Builds deterministic LNAV-like bit streams with valid GPS parity, creates
synthetic subframes, detects HOW/TOW evidence in hard-bit streams, and rebuilds
continuous LNAV streams from decoded source subframe templates.

\subsection synthetic app/dsp/synthetic_satellite.py

Contains the single-satellite augmentation path: input validation, complex64
file sizing, automatic amplitude estimation, compute backend selection, CPU/GPU
block synthesis, metadata generation, and detect-first planning.

\subsection tow app/dsp/tow_detect.py

Provides measurement TOW discovery. It first consumes sidecar metadata when
available, then tries Fraunhofer_FHR fast navigation decoding for long captures,
then falls back to a lightweight local acquisition/tracking/HOW scan.

\subsection relocation app/dsp/relocation_overlay.py

Builds and writes the position relocation overlay. It converts WGS-84
coordinates, calls Fraunhofer_FHR for baseline PVT and navigation evidence,
computes target pseudorange deltas, shifts LNAV arrival timing by whole
milliseconds for global relocations, preserves fractional C/A phase for the
remaining sub-millisecond delay, compensates carrier Doppler and Doppler drift,
compensates code-rate drift, and mixes multiple received-PRN replicas block by
block.

\section gui GUI Modules

\subsection mainwindow app/gui/main_window.py

Owns the PySide6 interface: input/output paths, synthetic satellite controls,
position-overlay controls, progress state, logging, worker lifecycle, and result
summaries.

\subsection workers app/gui/workers.py

Defines QThread workers for synthetic writing, detect-first planning,
relocation planning, and relocation writing. Workers expose progress, messages,
success, cancellation, and failure signals.

\section tests Tests

\subsection testgpsca app/tests/test_gps_ca.py

Checks PRN generation, reference C/A behavior, sampling, caching, and validation.

\subsection testlnav app/tests/test_lnav.py

Checks LNAV parity, HOW/TOW parsing, deterministic bit generation, and template
stream rebuilding.

\subsection testsynthetic app/tests/test_synthetic_satellite.py

Checks file augmentation, metadata payloads, auto amplitude, detection planning,
compute backend selection, cancellation cleanup, and invalid input handling.

\subsection testrelocation app/tests/test_relocation_overlay.py

Checks multi-PRN overlay writing, Fraunhofer-compatible pseudorange sign,
reference-sample rebasing, fractional code phase, and range-rate code-rate
compensation.

\subsection testgui app/tests/test_gui_smoke.py

Checks that the GUI constructs, important controls exist, and worker-facing
defaults remain usable without running long DSP jobs.

\section external Fraunhofer_FHR Interface

GPSDataAdder uses the sibling \c Fraunhofer_FHR repository as an offline decoder
oracle when it is present next to this project or configured through
\c FRAUNHOFER_FHR_PATH. The interface is intentionally one-way and offline:
GPSDataAdder launches small Python subprocesses inside Fraunhofer_FHR, receives
JSON evidence, and never imports long-running GUI state from that project.

The relocation overlay uses Fraunhofer_FHR for:

- acquisition ranking of received PRNs,
- tracking-loop code phase and code-rate evidence,
- LNAV bit and subframe decoding,
- ephemeris extraction,
- baseline PVT solution,
- apparent satellite position, velocity, and acceleration evidence.

\section build Build And Verification

Use the normal test and documentation commands from the repository root:

\code{.ps1}
pytest app/tests
doxygen Doxyfile
\endcode

The Doxygen command requires Doxygen to be installed on the machine. Generated
HTML stays local under \c docs/doxygen-output/html.

*/
